\DOC ACCUMULATE_ARITH_TAC

\TYPE {ACCUMULATE_ARITH_TAC : string -> tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Given a state-name string, rewrites one assumption describing a machine-word
arithmetic result for that state into a named abstract summand/carry form,
adding the corresponding arithmetic equation as a new assumption and leaving
the conclusion unchanged.

\DESCRIBE
The single unnamed argument is a {string} naming the state whose assumptions
are to be processed; in the observed traces it is supplied either as a plain
identifier or as an expression computing the name. The tactic selects one
assumption of {A} that expresses a register/flag/location value as a composite
word-arithmetic term for the named state and deletes it, and in some
applications also deletes a second assumption mentioning the same composite
term (typically a flag equivalence). It then appends new assumptions: an
arithmetic equation over {&}-injected values relating a fresh summand and carry
constant to the operands, together with reformulated readings of the affected
locations and flag in terms of those fresh constants. So, writing {z1 ... zp}
for the appended assumptions:
{
            A ?- t
   =============================  ACCUMULATE_ARITH_TAC s
           A' ?- t
}
\noindent where {A'} is {A} with one or two assumptions removed and one to
three replacement assumptions {z1 ... zp} appended; the conclusion {t} is
untouched and no case split occurs.

\FAILURE
Fails with a search exception, arising inside the tactic's own search over
candidate assumptions, when no assumption of the goal matches the pattern it
looks for under the supplied state name — e.g. when the assumptions for that
state contain no as-yet-unprocessed composite word-arithmetic result, or when
the state named by the argument is not the one described by the assumptions.

\COMMENTS
All observed traces show this single kind of transformation, always on goals
whose assumptions mention the supplied state name and whose conclusion is an
{eventually} machine-semantics statement.

\ENDDOC
